1
00:00:00,448 --> 00:00:01,331
This is Lugha.

2
00:00:02,081 --> 00:00:04,911
People in Nigeria earn dollars for small language tasks,

3
00:00:05,194 --> 00:00:07,822
and the money moves through an escrow contract on QDay

4
00:00:07,862 --> 00:00:08,388
Aevum.

5
00:00:10,048 --> 00:00:12,938
Lots of young Nigerians have a smartphone and free time,

6
00:00:13,137 --> 00:00:15,943
but no bank account that can receive a payment from abroad.

7
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:20,112
AI also handles Pidgin, Yoruba and Hausa badly,

8
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:23,021
because there is so little data in those languages.

9
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,725
Lugha pays people to make that data,

10
00:00:25,912 --> 00:00:27,315
in tUSD8.

11
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,033
Say I need Pidgin translations.

12
00:00:31,771 --> 00:00:34,844
I write three sentences, add one hidden check where I

13
00:00:34,884 --> 00:00:38,006
already know the answer, and pay two cents per answer.

14
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:42,651
When I publish, my wallet asks for one signature.

15
00:00:43,388 --> 00:00:45,930
I don't send a transaction and I pay no gas.

16
00:00:46,681 --> 00:00:49,454
The app relays the signature, and the contract pulls

17
00:00:49,494 --> 00:00:51,162
the whole budget into escrow.

18
00:00:52,804 --> 00:00:54,649
Here it is on the Aevum explorer.

19
00:00:55,386 --> 00:00:56,991
Our operator paid the gas.

20
00:00:57,718 --> 00:00:59,935
From now on the money sits in the contract,

21
00:01:00,266 --> 00:01:02,776
and nobody can take back what a worker has earned.

22
00:01:04,471 --> 00:01:06,267
Now the worker, on a phone.

23
00:01:07,065 --> 00:01:08,645
One tap makes an account:

24
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:11,785
a key that stays on the device, with no email and no

25
00:01:11,825 --> 00:01:15,294
phone number. The worker reads each sentence and types

26
00:01:15,334 --> 00:01:16,197
it in Pidgin.

27
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:20,933
To get paid, the worker creates a wallet on the phone,

28
00:01:21,072 --> 00:01:22,195
also in one tap.

29
00:01:22,969 --> 00:01:25,787
Accepted answers show up as locked in the escrow.

30
00:01:26,539 --> 00:01:29,129
That hold gives us a minute to catch cheaters:

31
00:01:29,399 --> 00:01:32,496
if someone fails a hidden check, the contract withholds

32
00:01:32,536 --> 00:01:35,022
the payment and the money goes back to the budget.

33
00:01:36,751 --> 00:01:39,569
When the hold ends, anyone can release the payment,

34
00:01:39,804 --> 00:01:42,045
so the worker doesn't even depend on us.

35
00:01:42,782 --> 00:01:45,520
The tUSD8 lands in the worker's wallet.

36
00:01:47,227 --> 00:01:49,095
Every step links to the explorer.

37
00:01:49,845 --> 00:01:52,569
This is the release, paid straight from the escrow to

38
00:01:52,609 --> 00:01:53,292
the worker.

39
00:01:54,943 --> 00:01:57,533
Back on my side, I download the dataset.

40
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:00,319
Its hash is written into the escrow,

41
00:02:00,494 --> 00:02:03,158
so anyone can check that the file I got is the file the

42
00:02:03,198 --> 00:02:06,040
workers made. Then I close the task,

43
00:02:06,275 --> 00:02:08,977
and everything nobody earned comes back to my wallet.

44
00:02:10,676 --> 00:02:13,554
The contract has no admin key and no upgrade path.

45
00:02:14,304 --> 00:02:16,714
The operator can only pay the task's fixed rate,

46
00:02:16,936 --> 00:02:18,793
to workers, inside the budget.

47
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:21,762
We cover that with 18 Foundry tests,

48
00:02:21,972 --> 00:02:24,889
including a fuzz test, and we ran the whole money path

49
00:02:24,929 --> 00:02:26,065
on the live testnet.

50
00:02:26,876 --> 00:02:29,770
Lugha is live now, and the code is on GitHub.
